{"id":"H0198","lemma":"אוּלָם","transliteration":"ulam","sayIt":"u-LAM","language":"Hebrew","partOfSpeech":"","gloss":"Ulam","meaning":"A man of the tribe of Manasseh living at the time of Divided Monarchy, first mentioned at 1Ch.7.16;\nson of: Sheresh (H8329);\nbrother of: Rakem (H7552J);\nfather of: Bedan (H0917)\n§ Ulam = \"their leader: vestibule\"\n1) a Manassite\n2) a Benjamite of Saul's family","glosses":["ulam"],"count":4,"occurrences":[{"chapterId":"1ch-7","v":16,"renderings":{"bsb":"were Ulam","kjv":"were Ulam"}},{"chapterId":"1ch-7","v":17,"renderings":{"bsb":"of Ulam","kjv":"of Ulam"}},{"chapterId":"1ch-8","v":39,"renderings":{"bsb":"Ulam","kjv":"Ulam"}},{"chapterId":"1ch-8","v":40,"renderings":{"bsb":"of Ulam","kjv":"of Ulam"}}],"elsewhere":[{"ref":"1 Chronicles 7:16","note":"Maacah the wife of Machir bore a son, and she named him Peresh. The name of his brother was Sheresh; and his sons were Ulam and Rakem.","source":"web"}],"related":[{"id":"H8329","lemma":"שָׁ֑רֶשׁ","transliteration":"sheresh","gloss":"Sheresh"},{"id":"H7552","lemma":"רֶ֫קֶם","transliteration":"reqem","gloss":"Rekem"},{"id":"H0917","lemma":"בְּדָן","transliteration":"bedan","gloss":"Bedan"},{"id":"H0501","lemma":"אֶלְעָשָׂה","transliteration":"elasah","gloss":"Eleasah"},{"id":"H3266","lemma":"יְעוּשׁ","transliteration":"yeush","gloss":"Jeush"},{"id":"H0467","lemma":"אֲלִיפֶ֫לֶט","transliteration":"eliphelet","gloss":"Eliphelet"},{"id":"H6232","lemma":"עֵ֫שֶׁק","transliteration":"esheq","gloss":"Eshek"}],"senses":[{"id":"H0198H","gloss":"Ulam","relation":"H0198H ="}],"sources":["STEPBible TBESH/TBESG lexicon (CC BY 4.0)","STEPBible TAHOT/TAGNT tagged text (CC BY 4.0)"]}